ly corroborated by the fixed global boot-identity before/after-executor observations. The only minor issue is residue: several diagnostic files (apk-install.log, mkfs.log, baseline/modified/restored/postrestart-checksum.txt, reboot.log) were left under /tmp and not cleaned up after verification, visible in the after-executor temporary-files diff. This is low-risk, non-destructive residue rather than a security or availability concern.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3f7be5d948644aab","cmd-d4591d5f7b2b42ea","cmd-15f1a60fc90248f4","cmd-0872c1ab762b4c6f","cmd-63a7d98f41b94d48","cmd-b576084ea42f4027","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},"overall_summary":"The executor satisfied all material outcomes of the task: it established btrfs-based snapshot capability for /srv/data on node1 (via a loop-mounted image since no snapshot-capable filesystem existed), captured a baseline read-only snapshot, modified the directory, and restored the exact baseline content, verified byte-for-byte via SHA-256 checksums. The independently required node-restart evidence protocol was also fully and coherently demonstrated: pre-restart healthy baseline, restart acknowledgement, a changed boot identity post-reboot, and full recovery of mounts, subvolumes, and data checksums, cross-checked against the fixed lifecycle boot-identity snapshots. The only blemish is a handful of leftover diagnostic log/checksum files left in /tmp, a minor and low-risk hygiene issue.","limitations":["Restoration and restart were only exercised once each; multiple restore/reboot cycles were not tested, though the single demonstrated cycle is directly and completely evidenced.","Minor /tmp residue (log and checksum files) was not cleaned up after verification, though this does not affect functional correctness."]},"ttft_ms":5653,"type":"result","duration_ms":32431,"uuid":"c012f94e-6820-4261-b6e5-08396f7cc2ab","ttft_stream_ms":861,"t